RISK

In real-world exploitation, heap out-of-bounds writes are a very powerful primitive that can lead to denial of service, privilege escalation, and arbitrary code execution.

REMEDIATION

Change the gint outlen variable in g_base64_encode to gsize to prevent calculation errors caused by mixing gint and gsize types.

